      "message": "This `willUpdate` block (and the identical copy in `gr-diff-lean-viewer.ts:1182-1259`) has grown very hard to follow with manual `changedProperties` diffing, self-mutation flags (`rowsChanged`, `internalThreadsUpdated`, `threadsInputsChanged`), and four `cached*` fields. We can simplify most of it:\n\n1. Subscribe directly to the context pref with `select(this.getUserModel().diffPreferences$, p \u003d\u003e p.context)` (or add `preferenceDiffContext$` on `UserModel`, like `preferenceDiffViewMode$`) instead of storing all of `diffPrefs` and diffing `changedProperties.get(\u0027diffPrefs\u0027)` in multiple branches.\n2. Drop the manual `willUpdate` cache invalidation for `attachThreadsToRows` and `groupRichDiffRows`. Neither hover nor text selection is `@state()`, so `render()` does not fire on mouse moves. If memoization is needed (for example on `collapseProofs` toggles in `gr-diff-lean-viewer`), a small input-reference memoizer or shared Lit `ReactiveController` avoids maintaining an 11-property `changedProperties` checklist and removes the duplication between both viewers.\n3. Clear selection/hover and reset `expandedRowIndices` directly in the action/subscription handlers rather than routing them through a multi-property `changedProperties` matrix and repeating the same reset in `recomputeAlignedRows()`. We can also drop the unused `context` prop and `toggleAllContext()` method on both viewers (neither has production callers outside unit tests).",
