      "message": "`tabindex\u003d\"-1\"` and `data-row-index` are wired into the `deleted`, `added`, and `modified` branches here and in `renderRightCell` (plus the same branches in `gr-diff-lean-viewer.ts`). Since any row with `status !\u003d\u003d \u0027unchanged\u0027` is always an anchor, it can never be collapsed or targeted by `focusRevealedRow()`. Putting `tabindex\u003d\"-1\"` on every diff block also makes every cell click-focusable (which is why `richDiffContextBarStyles` had to suppress focus rings on `.diff-cell` / `.unified-block`). Limiting `data-row-index` and `tabindex\u003d\"-1\"` to unchanged rows (or setting `tabindex\u003d\"-1\"` only on the revealed element when focusing) removes this template noise and the `isLeftEmpty` / `!row.leftBlock` guards.",
